# This is a Spartan page

You are reading this at spartan://localhost:13300/: served to you by the Unseen Servant (usv) Spartan server.

## Unseen Servant, and why "usv"

Unseen Servant is a small server that publishes one folder of writing to several internet protocols at once. The short name takes the letters from the long one:

```
UnSeen serVant  ->  u  s  v
```

It is abbreviated rather than spelled out because it is also a command you type.

## About Spartan

Spartan is Gemini's document model with the cryptography removed. Its argument is that mandatory TLS is ceremony for public documents: clocks that must be right, libraries that must be maintained, hardware that must do the maths, and that a plain document deserves a plain protocol. It reads the same gemtext.

=> http://portal.mozz.us/spartan/spartan.mozz.us/specification.gmi The Spartan specification

## Reading Spartan natively

If this page arrived looking strange, you may be reading it through a gateway. These clients speak Spartan directly:

=> https://gmi.skyjake.fi/lagrange/ Lagrange (graphical)
=> https://offpunk.net/ Offpunk (terminal)
=> https://git.sr.ht/~hedy/gelim gelim (terminal)
=> https://codeberg.org/luxferre/BFG BFG (terminal)

Client support changes; this list was checked in August 2026.

## The same writing, other protocols

This is one folder of writing, rendered to each of these. The hostname never changes, the scheme at the front picks the protocol and the port:

* Gemini: gemini://localhost:11965/
* Gopher: gopher://localhost:17070/
* Nex: nex://localhost:11900/
* Finger: finger://localhost:17979
* Web: https://localhost/

